module transfectionEfficiencyDetection
module knockoutDetection
module knockInDetection
module exhaustionPhenotypeDetection
module cytokineDetection

manifest DMFectionBuffer
manifest SurfactantF_Buffer
manifest CD4_T_Cells
manifest SpCas9_Nuclease
manifest TRAC_sgRNA
manifest NTC_sgRNA
manifest ExhaustionTarget_sgRNA
manifest EGFP_mRNA
manifest ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator
manifest IL2_200IU
manifest IL2_10IU
manifest BasalTCellMedia
manifest GFP_cssDNA_Template
manifest AntiHER2_CAR_dsDNA_Template
manifest ProteinL_Stain
manifest PE_LAG3_Stain
manifest FC_Oil

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Miniaturized Scalable Arrayed CRISPR Screening in Primary
// Cells Enables Discovery at the Single Donor Resolution
// Patel, Boribong et al., Scientific Reports (2025) 15:29350
// DOI: 10.1038/s41598-025-13532-z
//
// Platform: DropGenie DMF Transfection System (48-site array,
// SBS-format cartridge, Echo 655 acoustic liquid handler for
// guide deposition, Assist Plus 8-channel liquid handler for
// cell/payload loading and offloading).
//
// This file encodes three sequential protocol arms in the
// order presented in the paper:
//
// ARM 1 (BB1-BB4):  TRAC knockout in primary human CD4+ /
//                   CD8+ T cells. Validates high-efficiency
//                   RNP delivery at 10,000 cells/edit.
//                   (Fig. 2B; ~90% TCR alpha/beta KO,
//                   >95% viability.)
//
// ARM 2 (BB5-BB8):  GFP knock-in at the TRAC locus using
//                   a circular single-stranded DNA (cssDNA)
//                   template (4 kb). Validates HDR delivery
//                   at 10,000 cells/edit.
//                   (Fig. 2D; ~52% GFP+ at 500V/2ms/2pulses.)
//
// ARM 3 (BB9-BB14): Arrayed CRISPR-Cas9 exhaustion screen
//                   in chronically stimulated primary human
//                   CD4+ T cells. 45 targets screened
//                   (192 edits total), 10,000 cells/condition.
//                   Readouts: LAG-3 surface expression,
//                   IFNgamma, TNFalpha secretion (ELISA).
//                   Top hits: SIN3A, PAF1, PRDM1, SETBP1,
//                   STAT1. (Fig. 3.)
//
// DROPLET / CELL LOADING ABSTRACTION:
//   All `mix` steps at the loading stage abstract the
//   Assist Plus 8-channel pipette loading operation into
//   the DropGenie cartridge (100 uL per well), not a
//   bulk-reagent mixing event. The DropGenie cartridge
//   uses Tri-Drop Electroporation: two conductive buffer
//   (DMFection Buffer) droplets flank a central cell/cargo
//   droplet; electrode actuation forms a transient low-
//   current electroporation zone.
//
// ELECTROPORATION PARAMETERS (all arms):
//   T cell KO (Pan CD3+):   500 V, 3 ms, 2 pulses, 5 min incubation
//   T cell KO (CD4+/Treg):  550 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses, 5 min incubation
//   T cell knock-in:         500 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses
//   Exhaustion screen:       550 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses
//   BioScript `heat` steps model the post-load incubation
//   period at 37 C before the electrode pulse sequence fires.
//   Pulse delivery itself is instantaneous and is abstracted
//   into the `mix` (loading/merge) step.
//
// RNP AMOUNTS PER EDIT (T cells, ARM 1 and ARM 3):
//   SpCas9:  0.42 pmol  (ARM 1 KO) / 1 pmol (ARM 3 screen)
//   sgRNA:   2.1  pmol  (ARM 1 KO) / 2 pmol (ARM 3 screen)
//   Cells:   10,000 per edit
//   Volume:  100 uL loaded per cartridge well
//   vs. conventional: 500,000 cells, 50 pmol sgRNA, 100 pmol Cas9
//   Reduction: 50x cells, ~25x sgRNA, ~100x Cas9 (Fig. 3G)
//
// GUIDE PRE-DEPOSITION (all arms):
//   sgRNAs are deposited dry onto the DropGenie substrate in
//   40 nL spots by the Echo 655 acoustic liquid handler,
//   mixed with Poly-L-glutamic acid (PGA) as a carrier, then
//   desiccated before cartridge assembly. The `dispense`
//   statements for sgRNA manifest this pre-deposition as a
//   unit-volume dispense event; BioScript has no native
//   acoustic dispense primitive.
//
// CELL ACTIVATION (pre-protocol, off-chip):
//   CD4+ T cells are thawed and cultured at 1.25e6 cells/mL
//   in Basal T Cell Media + 400 IU/mL IL-2 + 25 ng/mL IL-7
//   + 50 ng/mL IL-15 for 3 days prior to transfection.
//   This activation step is encoded as the first `heat`
//   step (37 C, 4320 min = 3 days) before cartridge loading.
//
// EXHAUSTION INDUCTION (ARM 3 only):
//   Post-KO, CD4+ T cells are re-stimulated every 3 days
//   with ImmunoCult CD3/CD28 + 10 IU/mL IL-2 for 28 days
//   to model chronic T cell exhaustion in vitro.
//   Each 3-day re-stimulation cycle encoded as:
//     heat at 37c for 4320m (3 days = 4320 min).
//   Nine cycles cover the full 28-day exhaustion window
//   (9 x 3 days = 27 days + terminal Day 28 assay readout).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- T cell activation; ARM 1 TRAC KO
//                            cartridge loading; electroporation;
//                            post-KO culture
//   BB2  knockoutPass      -- knockoutSignal > 0: >80% TCR KO;
//                            dispose; proceed to ARM 2
//   BB3  knockoutFail      -- knockoutSignal <= 0: low KO; drain
//   BB4  knockoutJoin      -- join: ARM 2 (knock-in) begins
//   BB5  knockInPass       -- knockInSignal > 0: GFP+ detected;
//                            dispose; proceed to ARM 3
//   BB6  knockInFail       -- knockInSignal <= 0: no GFP+; drain
//   BB7  knockInJoin       -- join: ARM 3 (screen) begins
//   BB8  screenSetup       -- screen RNP assembly and loading
//                            (inline -- no branch; part of main
//                            before exhaustion induction)
//   BB9  exhaustionLoop    -- 9x chronic re-stimulation cycles
//                            (unrolled; BioScript has no loop
//                            primitive; see NOTE below)
//   BB10 assayReadout      -- LAG-3 and cytokine detection
//   BB11 screenPass        -- screenSignal > 0: escape hits
//                            detected; dispose
//   BB12 screenFail        -- screenSignal <= 0: no escape; drain
//   BB13 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
//
// NOTE ON LOOP UNROLLING:
//   BioScript (lilott8/BioScript) does not support `repeat`
//   or `while` loop constructs. The 9 chronic re-stimulation
//   cycles are therefore unrolled as 9 sequential `mix` +
//   `heat` pairs. Each pair models one 3-day stimulation
//   cycle (ImmunoCult + IL-2 addition, 37 C for 4320 min).
//   This is the same unrolling strategy used in reference
//   BioScript files for multi-step incubation protocols.
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PRE-PROTOCOL: T cell activation (off-chip, 3 days).
//   CD4+ T cells thawed into Basal T Cell Media + cytokines.
//   Cultured at 37 C / 5% CO2 for 72 h before transfection.
//   `heat` abstracts the 3-day activation incubation
//   (3 days = 4320 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

basalMedia      = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2Stock        = dispense 1 units of IL2_200IU
activator       = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator
cd4Cells        = dispense 1 units of CD4_T_Cells

activationMedia = mix basalMedia with il2Stock for 5s
activationMix   = mix activationMedia with activator for 5s
activatedCells  = mix cd4Cells with activationMix for 5s

// 3-day activation at 37 C / 5% CO2 (3 days = 4320 min).
heat activatedCells at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 1: Prepare Transfection Buffer (cell wash).
//   Cells washed in DMFection Buffer then resuspended in
//   Transfection Buffer (0.01% Surfactant F in DMFection
//   Buffer) at 1.0e7 cells/mL before cartridge loading.
//   `mix` abstracts the wash and resuspension step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dmfBuffer1      = dispense 1 units of DMFectionBuffer
surfactantBuf1  = dispense 1 units of SurfactantF_Buffer

transfectionBuf1 = mix dmfBuffer1 with surfactantBuf1 for 5s
cellSuspension1  = mix activatedCells with transfectionBuf1 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 2: Pre-deposit TRAC sgRNA dry onto substrate
//   via Echo 655 (40 nL spots, sgRNA + PGA carrier).
//   SpCas9 loaded into cartridge wells with cells.
//   `mix` abstracts cartridge well loading via Assist Plus.
//   Each edit: 10,000 cells, 2.1 pmol TRAC sgRNA (pre-dry),
//   0.42 pmol SpCas9, 100 uL total volume.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tracSgRNA1      = dispense 1 units of TRAC_sgRNA
cas9Load1       = dispense 1 units of SpCas9_Nuclease

rnpMix1         = mix tracSgRNA1 with cas9Load1 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 3: Load cells + RNP onto DropGenie cartridge.
//   Incubate 5 min at room temperature (pre-pulse incubation).
//   `heat` at 25 C for 5 min models the 5 min incubation
//   before electrode pulse delivery.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cartridgeLoad1  = mix cellSuspension1 with rnpMix1 for 5s

// 5-min pre-pulse incubation at room temperature (25 C).
heat cartridgeLoad1 at 25c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 4: Electroporation (550 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses).
//   FC_Oil filler droplets abstract the Tri-Drop flanking
//   buffer droplets that complete the electroporation circuit.
//   `mix` with FC_Oil models droplet merge / circuit formation
//   on the electrode array. The actual pulse is abstracted
//   into this merge event.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilBuffer1      = dispense 1 units of FC_Oil

electroporatedCells1 = mix cartridgeLoad1 with oilBuffer1 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 5: Offload and post-KO culture (3 days).
//   Cells offloaded into Basal T Cell Media + 200 IU/mL IL-2
//   in a 96-well round-bottom plate via Assist Plus.
//   Cultured 72 h at 37 C / 5% CO2 before flow cytometry.
//   (3 days = 4320 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

recoveryMedia1  = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2Recovery1    = dispense 1 units of IL2_200IU

recoveryMix1    = mix recoveryMedia1 with il2Recovery1 for 5s
kulturedCells1  = mix electroporatedCells1 with recoveryMix1 for 5s

// 72 h post-KO culture at 37 C / 5% CO2.
heat kulturedCells1 at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 6: KO detection via flow cytometry.
//   knockoutDetection module abstracts TCR alpha/beta surface
//   staining and flow cytometry analysis (Attune NxT).
//   Readout: % TCR alpha/beta-negative cells in CD4+ and
//   CD8+ subsets. Target: >80% TCR KO (paper: 90.41% CD4+,
//   91.87% CD8+; viability >97%).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

knockoutSignal  = detect knockoutDetection on kulturedCells1 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: TRAC KO QC gate
// Pass (BB2): knockoutSignal > 0 -> >80% TCR alpha/beta KO
//             confirmed; dispose cells; proceed to ARM 2.
// Fail (BB3): knockoutSignal <= 0 -> insufficient KO
//             (e.g. guide failure, electroporation fault);
//             drain and do not proceed.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (knockoutJoin).
// ============================================================

if (knockoutSignal > 0) {
    dispose kulturedCells1
} else {
    drain kulturedCells1
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: knockoutJoin
// Dispose KO QC signal. Control falls into ARM 2 (knock-in).
// ============================================================

dispose knockoutSignal

// ============================================================
// ARM 2: GFP Knock-In at TRAC Locus via cssDNA HDR Template
// (Fig. 2D; 10,000 Pan CD3+ T cells/edit, 4 kb GFP cssDNA,
//  0.03-0.06 ug template/edit, 500 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses,
//  10-day expansion, ~52% GFP+ at 0.03 ug/500V/2ms/2pulses)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BB5 - ARM 2, STEP 1: T cell activation (separate donor,
//   Dynabead CD3/CD28 protocol for knock-in experiments).
//   Pan CD3+ T cells activated 3 days at 37 C.
//   Dynabeads removed before transfection (off-chip).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

basalMedia2     = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2KI           = dispense 1 units of IL2_200IU
cd3Cells2       = dispense 1 units of CD4_T_Cells

activationMix2  = mix basalMedia2 with il2KI for 5s
activatedCells2 = mix cd3Cells2 with activationMix2 for 5s

// 3-day Dynabead activation at 37 C (3 days = 4320 min).
heat activatedCells2 at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 2: Prepare Transfection Buffer for KI run.
//   Cells resuspended at 1.0e7 cells/mL in Transfection Buffer.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dmfBuffer2      = dispense 1 units of DMFectionBuffer
surfactantBuf2  = dispense 1 units of SurfactantF_Buffer

transfectionBuf2 = mix dmfBuffer2 with surfactantBuf2 for 5s
cellSuspension2  = mix activatedCells2 with transfectionBuf2 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 3: Assemble TRAC RNP for KI experiment.
//   110 pmol TRAC sgRNA + 33 pmol SpCas9, complexed on ice
//   for 20 min. Per edit: 1.1 pmol sgRNA, 0.33 pmol Cas9.
//   `heat` at 4 C for 20 min models on-ice RNP assembly.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tracSgRNA2      = dispense 1 units of TRAC_sgRNA
cas9Load2       = dispense 1 units of SpCas9_Nuclease

rnpAssembly2    = mix tracSgRNA2 with cas9Load2 for 5s

// 20 min on-ice RNP complexing (4 C, 20 min).
heat rnpAssembly2 at 4c for 20m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 4: Add GFP cssDNA template to cartridge load.
//   0.03 ug GFP cssDNA (circular single-stranded DNA) per edit.
//   cssDNA from Full Circles Therapeutics; provides improved
//   intracellular stability and targeted genomic integration
//   efficiency vs dsDNA.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gfpTemplate     = dispense 1 units of GFP_cssDNA_Template

rnpTemplateMix2 = mix rnpAssembly2 with gfpTemplate for 5s
cartridgeLoad2  = mix cellSuspension2 with rnpTemplateMix2 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 5: Electroporation (500 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses).
//   Tri-Drop circuit formation abstracted as mix with FC_Oil.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilBuffer2      = dispense 1 units of FC_Oil

electroporatedCells2 = mix cartridgeLoad2 with oilBuffer2 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 6: Offload and 10-day expansion.
//   Cells offloaded into Basal T Cell Media + 300 IU/mL IL-2.
//   10-day culture at 37 C / 5% CO2 before flow cytometry
//   and fluorescence microscopy readout.
//   (10 days = 14400 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

recoveryMedia2  = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2Recovery2    = dispense 1 units of IL2_200IU

recoveryMix2    = mix recoveryMedia2 with il2Recovery2 for 5s
kulturedCells2  = mix electroporatedCells2 with recoveryMix2 for 5s

// 10-day expansion at 37 C (10 days = 14400 min).
heat kulturedCells2 at 37c for 14400m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 7: GFP knock-in detection via flow cytometry.
//   knockInDetection module abstracts GFP positivity gating
//   (Attune NxT; TRAC KO co-stain to confirm on-target HDR).
//   Expected: ~52% GFP+ cells at 0.03 ug / 500V / 2ms / 2p.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

knockInSignal   = detect knockInDetection on kulturedCells2 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: KI QC gate
// Pass (BB5): knockInSignal > 0 -> GFP+ cells confirmed
//             (HDR successful); dispose; proceed to ARM 3.
// Fail (BB6): knockInSignal <= 0 -> no GFP integration;
//             drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (knockInJoin).
// ============================================================

if (knockInSignal > 0) {
    dispose kulturedCells2
} else {
    drain kulturedCells2
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: knockInJoin
// Dispose KI QC signal. Control falls into ARM 3 (screen).
// ============================================================

dispose knockInSignal

// ============================================================
// ARM 3: Arrayed CRISPR-Cas9 Exhaustion Screen
// 45 targets x 4 replicates = 192 edits on DropGenie array.
// 10,000 CD4+ T cells / edit, 2 pmol sgRNA, 1 pmol Cas9.
// 28-day chronic stimulation model, LAG-3 + cytokine readout.
// (Fig. 3; top hits: SIN3A, PAF1, PRDM1, SETBP1, STAT1)
//
// This arm encodes one representative screen condition
// (ExhaustionTarget_sgRNA) in full. The same cartridge
// loading, electroporation, and exhaustion induction workflow
// is applied in parallel across all 48 addressable sites of
// the DropGenie cartridge per run (4 runs for 192 edits).
// Parallelism is abstracted here as sequential BioScript
// statements, consistent with the reference .bs files.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BB8 - ARM 3, STEP 1: CD4+ T cell activation (screen donor).
//   CD4+ Helper T cells (AllCells) thawed and activated:
//   1.25e6 cells/mL, Basal T Cell Media + 400 IU/mL IL-2 +
//   25 ng/mL IL-7 + 50 ng/mL IL-15, 3 days at 37 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

basalMedia3     = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2Screen       = dispense 1 units of IL2_200IU
cd4Cells3       = dispense 1 units of CD4_T_Cells

activationMix3  = mix basalMedia3 with il2Screen for 5s
activatedCells3 = mix cd4Cells3 with activationMix3 for 5s

// 3-day activation at 37 C (3 days = 4320 min).
heat activatedCells3 at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 2: Prepare Transfection Buffer (screen).
//   Cells washed and resuspended at 1.0e7 cells/mL in
//   Transfection Buffer. Echo 655 pre-deposits ExhaustionTarget
//   sgRNA + PGA (40 nL / site) onto substrate before assembly.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dmfBuffer3      = dispense 1 units of DMFectionBuffer
surfactantBuf3  = dispense 1 units of SurfactantF_Buffer

transfectionBuf3 = mix dmfBuffer3 with surfactantBuf3 for 5s
cellSuspension3  = mix activatedCells3 with transfectionBuf3 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 3: Assemble screen RNP.
//   ExhaustionTarget_sgRNA pre-deposited dry on substrate.
//   SpCas9 loaded into cartridge wells with cells.
//   Per edit: 10,000 cells, 2 pmol sgRNA, 1 pmol Cas9,
//   100 uL total volume.
//   RNP complexing occurs in situ on the cartridge during
//   the 5-min pre-pulse incubation (modelled as heat 25 C, 5m).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

screenSgRNA     = dispense 1 units of ExhaustionTarget_sgRNA
cas9Screen      = dispense 1 units of SpCas9_Nuclease

screenRnpMix    = mix screenSgRNA with cas9Screen for 5s
cartridgeLoad3  = mix cellSuspension3 with screenRnpMix for 5s

// 5-min pre-pulse incubation at room temperature (25 C).
heat cartridgeLoad3 at 25c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 4: Electroporation (550 V, 2 ms, 2 pulses).
//   Tri-Drop circuit formation abstracted as mix with FC_Oil.
//   DropGenie fires each of the 48 sites independently under
//   user-defined parameters set via the instrument software.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilBuffer3      = dispense 1 units of FC_Oil

electroporatedCells3 = mix cartridgeLoad3 with oilBuffer3 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 5: Offload and 3-day initial recovery.
//   Cells offloaded into Basal T Cell Media + 200 IU/mL IL-2
//   (96-well round-bottom plate via Assist Plus).
//   3-day recovery culture before exhaustion induction begins.
//   (3 days = 4320 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

recoveryMedia3  = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2Recovery3    = dispense 1 units of IL2_200IU

recoveryMix3    = mix recoveryMedia3 with il2Recovery3 for 5s
recoveredCells3 = mix electroporatedCells3 with recoveryMix3 for 5s

// 3-day initial recovery at 37 C.
heat recoveredCells3 at 37c for 4320m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEPS 6-14: Chronic re-stimulation for exhaustion
//   induction (9 cycles x 3 days = 27 days, Days 3-30).
//
//   Protocol: ImmunoCult CD3/CD28 (25 uL/mL) + 10 IU/mL IL-2
//   in 50 uL Basal T Cell Media, media change every 3 days.
//   This recapitulates progressive T cell dysfunction in vivo
//   (chronic antigen exposure model).
//
//   BioScript has no loop primitive; 9 cycles unrolled below.
//   Each cycle: dispense fresh stimulation media, mix with
//   cells, heat 37 C for 4320 min (3 days).
//
//   NOTE: ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator manifest is reused
//   across cycles (same reagent, fresh aliquot each media
//   change). IL2_10IU manifest = 10 IU/mL IL-2 stock (lower
//   concentration than activation arm; paper M&M specifies
//   10 IU/mL for exhaustion induction vs 200 IU/mL activation).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 1 (Days 3-6) --
stimMedia_c1    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c1          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c1    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c1      = mix stimMedia_c1 with il2_c1 for 5s
stimMix_c1b     = mix stimMix_c1 with activator_c1 for 5s
stimCells_c1    = mix recoveredCells3 with stimMix_c1b for 5s
heat stimCells_c1 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 2 (Days 6-9) --
stimMedia_c2    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c2          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c2    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c2      = mix stimMedia_c2 with il2_c2 for 5s
stimMix_c2b     = mix stimMix_c2 with activator_c2 for 5s
stimCells_c2    = mix stimCells_c1 with stimMix_c2b for 5s
heat stimCells_c2 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 3 (Days 9-12) --
stimMedia_c3    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c3          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c3    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c3      = mix stimMedia_c3 with il2_c3 for 5s
stimMix_c3b     = mix stimMix_c3 with activator_c3 for 5s
stimCells_c3    = mix stimCells_c2 with stimMix_c3b for 5s
heat stimCells_c3 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 4 (Days 12-15) --
stimMedia_c4    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c4          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c4    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c4      = mix stimMedia_c4 with il2_c4 for 5s
stimMix_c4b     = mix stimMix_c4 with activator_c4 for 5s
stimCells_c4    = mix stimCells_c3 with stimMix_c4b for 5s
heat stimCells_c4 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 5 (Days 15-18) --
stimMedia_c5    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c5          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c5    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c5      = mix stimMedia_c5 with il2_c5 for 5s
stimMix_c5b     = mix stimMix_c5 with activator_c5 for 5s
stimCells_c5    = mix stimCells_c4 with stimMix_c5b for 5s
heat stimCells_c5 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 6 (Days 18-21) --
stimMedia_c6    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c6          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c6    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c6      = mix stimMedia_c6 with il2_c6 for 5s
stimMix_c6b     = mix stimMix_c6 with activator_c6 for 5s
stimCells_c6    = mix stimCells_c5 with stimMix_c6b for 5s
heat stimCells_c6 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 7 (Days 21-24) --
stimMedia_c7    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c7          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c7    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c7      = mix stimMedia_c7 with il2_c7 for 5s
stimMix_c7b     = mix stimMix_c7 with activator_c7 for 5s
stimCells_c7    = mix stimCells_c6 with stimMix_c7b for 5s
heat stimCells_c7 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 8 (Days 24-27) --
stimMedia_c8    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c8          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c8    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c8      = mix stimMedia_c8 with il2_c8 for 5s
stimMix_c8b     = mix stimMix_c8 with activator_c8 for 5s
stimCells_c8    = mix stimCells_c7 with stimMix_c8b for 5s
heat stimCells_c8 at 37c for 4320m

// -- Exhaustion Cycle 9 / Final Re-stimulation (Days 27-28) --
// Day 26 (paper): cells re-stimulated for 48 h before
// supernatant collection and final flow cytometry on Day 28.
// 48 h final stimulation = 2880 min.
stimMedia_c9    = dispense 1 units of BasalTCellMedia
il2_c9          = dispense 1 units of IL2_10IU
activator_c9    = dispense 1 units of ImmunoCult_CD3CD28_Activator

stimMix_c9      = mix stimMedia_c9 with il2_c9 for 5s
stimMix_c9b     = mix stimMix_c9 with activator_c9 for 5s
stimCells_c9    = mix stimCells_c8 with stimMix_c9b for 5s

// Final 48 h re-stimulation at 37 C before assay readout.
heat stimCells_c9 at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 15: LAG-3 exhaustion phenotype detection.
//   exhaustionPhenotypeDetection module abstracts:
//     1. PE-LAG3 surface staining (BioLegend)
//     2. Ghost Dye Violet 510 viability staining
//     3. CD4 co-stain (lineage gate)
//     4. Attune NxT flow cytometry analysis
//   Readout: % LAG3-negative CD4+ T cells (exhaustion escape).
//   screenSignal > 0 if LAG3- frequency > NTC control mean.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lag3Stain       = dispense 1 units of PE_LAG3_Stain
stainedForFACS  = mix stimCells_c9 with lag3Stain for 20m

screenSignal    = detect exhaustionPhenotypeDetection on stainedForFACS for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: Screen assay QC gate (LAG-3 readout)
// Pass (BB10): screenSignal > 0 -> LAG3- frequency above
//              NTC baseline; candidate escape hit confirmed;
//              proceed to cytokine validation branch.
// Fail (BB11): screenSignal <= 0 -> no exhaustion rescue;
//              drain.
// Both branches converge at BB12 before cytokine dispose.
// ============================================================

if (screenSignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedForFACS
} else {
    drain stainedForFACS
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 16: Cytokine secretion readout (ELISA).
//   Supernatants collected 48 h after final re-stimulation
//   (Day 28) and assayed for IFNgamma and TNFalpha by
//   sandwich ELISA (RayBiotech kits).
//   4PL regression used to interpolate concentrations.
//   Background subtracted using media-only (MO) control.
//   cytokineDetection module abstracts ELISA plate reader
//   readout and signal normalisation.
//   This step runs regardless of LAG-3 gate outcome to
//   capture composite exhaustion escape score data
//   (z-score of IFNy + TNFa + %LAG3- per Fig. 3F/S5C).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cytokineSignal  = detect cytokineDetection on screenSignal for 60s

// ============================================================
// BB13: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose both QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends; data passed to composite escape scoring
// pipeline (off-chip; z-score normalization, radar plot).
// ============================================================

dispose cytokineSignal
dispose screenSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
